manifold (3D mesh boolean kernel, C++), by Emmett Lalish and contributors; with its C binding
(manifoldc) and Clipper2 (Angus Johnson, Boost Software License 1.0, fetched by manifold's cmake).
URL:     https://github.com/elalish/manifold
Tag:     v3.5.3 (commit 0edd9d54876f3135e431575214dd6d8a72866fee), the version the Rust side
         links through the manifold-csg-sys 3.5.105 crate (its build.rs MANIFOLD_VERSION).
         deps.sh checks the clone's commit (MANIFOLD_COMMIT) and, after the configure, the
         Clipper2 commit that manifold's cmake fetched (CLIPPER2_COMMIT
         46f639177fe418f9689e8ddb74f08a870c71f5b4, pinned by cmake/manifoldDeps.cmake at that
         commit, with manifold's carry patch 0001-clipper2-no-iostream.patch).
Licence: Apache License 2.0 (manifold); Boost 1.0 (Clipper2). Both allow static linking into
         Bimble (MIT); a binary distribution carries their licence texts and NOTICE.
Files:   none committed here (no sources, no binaries). ccore/deps.sh clones the tag and builds it
         with cmake (the crate's options: CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release, MANIFOLD_CBIND=ON,
         MANIFOLD_CROSS_SECTION=ON, MANIFOLD_USE_BUILTIN_CLIPPER2=ON, MANIFOLD_PAR=OFF (no TBB),
         BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF, CMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON, tests and bindings off) into
         ccore/out/deps/manifold/, or, with MANIFOLD_DIR set, takes the libraries of an existing
         build (e.g. the crate's cargo output). It also links a libmanifoldc.so from the static
         libraries for tcc, which cannot link C++ static archives.
Local changes: none (the crate applies no carry patches at this version).
Used by: ccore/src/boolean.c (CC_HAVE_MANIFOLD), through the C binding only. wasm32: not built
         (freestanding, no C++ runtime): no kernel there, openings and boolean results are drawn
         uncut with a warning.
